# Testing, Logging & Observability Rules

## Testing Stack
- **Unit**: Jest + `@jest/globals`
- **Integration**: Jest + `supertest` (Express endpoints)
- **DB Integration**: Use test containers (`testcontainers`) or in-memory mocks
- **Coverage target**: ≥ 80% lines; 100% on all service-layer business logic

## Test File Conventions
- Co-locate unit tests: `src/services/__tests__/user-service.test.js`
- Integration tests: `tests/integration/user-api.test.js`
- Test factories: `tests/factories/user-factory.js`

## Unit Test Rules
- Mock all external dependencies (DB, ASB, HTTP calls) — never hit real services in unit tests.
- Follow **AAA pattern**: Arrange → Act → Assert.
- One assertion concept per `it()` block.
- Use `jest.spyOn` over manual mocks when possible.

```js
// tests/unit/user-service.test.js
import { describe, it, expect, jest, beforeEach } from '@jest/globals';
import { UserService } from '../../src/services/user-service.js';

describe('UserService', () => {
  let userService, userRepo, notifier;

  beforeEach(() => {
    userRepo = { findById: jest.fn(), create: jest.fn() };
    notifier = { send: jest.fn() };
    userService = new UserService(userRepo, notifier);
  });

  describe('createUser()', () => {
    it('should create a user and send a welcome notification', async () => {
      // Arrange
      const input    = { name: 'Alice', email: 'alice@example.com' };
      const created  = { id: 1, ...input };
      userRepo.create.mockResolvedValue(created);

      // Act
      const result = await userService.createUser(input);

      // Assert
      expect(userRepo.create).toHaveBeenCalledWith(input);
      expect(notifier.send).toHaveBeenCalledWith(expect.objectContaining({ to: input.email }));
      expect(result).toEqual(created);
    });

    it('should throw ValidationError for duplicate email', async () => {
      userRepo.create.mockRejectedValue({ code: 'ER_DUP_ENTRY' });
      await expect(userService.createUser({ email: 'dup@x.com' }))
        .rejects.toMatchObject({ code: 'VALIDATION_ERROR' });
    });
  });
});
```

## Integration Test Rules
- Use `supertest` against the Express `app` (not a running server).
- Seed and tear down test data in `beforeAll`/`afterAll`.
- Run integration tests against a **separate test database** (`.env.test`).

```js
// tests/integration/user-api.test.js
import request from 'supertest';
import app from '../../src/app.js';

describe('POST /api/v1/users', () => {
  it('returns 201 with created user', async () => {
    const res = await request(app)
      .post('/api/v1/users')
      .set('X-Request-Id', 'test-req-001')
      .send({ name: 'Bob', email: 'bob@example.com' });

    expect(res.status).toBe(201);
    expect(res.body.success).toBe(true);
    expect(res.body.data).toMatchObject({ name: 'Bob', email: 'bob@example.com' });
  });
});
```

